\id XXA emerald-tablet
\usfm 3.1
\ide UTF-8
\rem anagnosis work=emerald-tablet edition=steele.en lang=en urn=urn:cts:anagnosis:hermetica.emeraldtablet.steele-eng cite=vp
\rem source Wikipedia, "Emerald Tablet" (Steele & Singer 1928)
\rem rights Public domain
\h Emerald Tablet
\toc1 Emerald Tablet
\mt1 Emerald Tablet
\c 1
\p
\v 1 \vp 1\vp* True it is, without falsehood, certain and most true.
\v 2 \vp 2\vp* That which is above is like to that which is below, and that which is below is like to that which is above,
\v 3 \vp 3\vp* to accomplish the miracles of one thing.
\v 4 \vp 4\vp* And as all things were by contemplation of one, so all things arose from this one thing by a single act of adaptation.
\v 5 \vp 5\vp* The father thereof is the Sun, the mother the Moon.
\v 6 \vp 6\vp* The wind carried it in its womb, the earth is the nurse thereof.
\v 7 \vp 7\vp* It is the father of all works of wonder throughout the whole world.
\v 8 \vp 8\vp* The power thereof is perfect.
\v 9 \vp 9\vp* If it be cast on to earth, it will separate the element of earth from that of fire, the subtle from the gross.
\v 10 \vp 10\vp* With great sagacity it doth ascend gently from earth to heaven. Again it doth descend to earth,
\v 11 \vp 11\vp* and uniteth in itself the force from things superior and things inferior.
\v 12 \vp 12\vp* Thus thou wilt possess the glory of the brightness of the whole world, and all obscurity will fly far from thee.
\v 13 \vp 13\vp* This thing is the strong fortitude of all strength,
\v 14 \vp 14\vp* for it overcometh every subtle thing and doth penetrate every solid substance.
\v 15 \vp 15\vp* Thus was this world created.
\v 16 \vp 16\vp* Hence will there be marvellous adaptations achieved, of which the manner is this.
\v 17 \vp 17\vp* For this reason I am called Hermes Trismegistus, because I hold three parts of the wisdom of the whole world.
\v 18 \vp 18\vp* That which I had to say about the operation of Sol is completed.
